msgstr "Referencia de la línea de comandos"

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:4
msgid ""
"The ``guidedog`` executable creates, builds, previews, translates, "
"converts, and publishes documentation projects. Its commands and options "
"follow ``sphinx-quickstart``, ``sphinx-build`` and ``sphinx-intl`` where "
"those have an equivalent. Existing habits and scripts carry over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:10
msgid "General syntax"
msgstr "Sintaxis general"

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:21
msgid ""
"Options may come before or after the arguments. ``--`` ends the options: "
"every word after it is an argument, even one that starts with ``-``. A "
"lone ``-`` is an argument (standard input or output, where a command "
"accepts it). A long option takes its value as ``--name=VALUE`` or as the "
"next word, ``--name VALUE``."
msgstr ""

